:HELP NAME='FLD/UPAUDLVL'.Action auditing values
:P.The action auditing values shown for what the display is about.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='KEYS/WRKKEYS'.Function keys
:PARML.
:PT.F3=Exit
:PD.Ends the display and returns to where it was started from.
:PT.F5=Refresh
:PD.Shows the display again with the current information.
:PT.F12=Cancel
:PD.Returns to the previous display without acting on what was typed.
:PT.F16=Repeat position to
:PD.Repeat position to.
:PT.F17=Position to
:PD.Positions the list at the name typed on the command line.
:PT.F21=Select assistance level
:PD.Select assistance level.
:PT.F24=More keys
:PD.Shows the other function keys of the display.
:PT.F6=Create
:PD.Runs CRTUSRPRF.
:PT.F9=Retrieve
:PD.Puts the last command run back on the command line; press it again
for the one before.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKUSRPRF/OPT'.Option
:P.Type the number of an option next to an entry and press Enter. The
options the list allows are shown above it; F1 on one of them explains
it.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/WUPNAME'.User Profile
:P.The user Profile of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='FLD/WUPTEXT'.Text
:P.The text of each entry in the list.
:EHELP.
:HELP NAME='WRKUSRPRF/OPTIONS'.Options
:P.Type an option number next to one or more entries and press Enter.
The option runs for each entry it is typed next to, in order.
:PARML.
:PT.1=Create
:PD.Type 1 next to an entry and press Enter to create it. The Create
User Profile (CRTUSRPRF) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.2=Change
:PD.Type 2 next to an entry and press Enter to change it. The Change
User Profile (CHGUSRPRF) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.3=Copy
:PD.Type 3 next to an entry and press Enter to copy it. The Create User
Profile (CRTUSRPRF) command is prompted for the entry.
:PT.4=Delete
:PD.Type 4 next to an entry and press Enter to delete it. The Delete
User Profile (DLTUSRPRF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.5=Display
:PD.Type 5 next to an entry and press Enter to display it. The Display
User Profile (DSPUSRPRF) command runs for the entry.
:PT.12=Work with objects by owner
:PD.Type 12 next to an entry and press Enter to work with objects by
owner it. The Work with Objects by Owner (WRKOBJOWN) command runs for
the entry.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
